# Whole-structure assignment to and from an array element.
#
# Derivation: assigning a structured variable copies its value, so a later
# write to the source or to the copy changes neither the other (ed.3 7.3.2.1,
# 6.4.4.2; ed.2 3.3.2.1); an element of an array of structures is such a
# variable (ed.3 6.4.4.3, 7.3.1). pts starts at (0, 0) everywhere (ed.3
# table 10) and keeps its value between cycles. Each cycle sets
# pts[i] = (k, 10*i) and c = (k, 10*i + 1), so cs = k + 10*i + 1:
#   cycle 0: i=1 k=3  -> pts[1] = (3, 10):  s1 13 s2 0  s3 0,  cs 14
#   cycle 1: i=3 k=-2 -> pts[3] = (-2, 30): s1 13 s2 0  s3 28, cs 29
#   cycle 2: i=1 k=5  -> pts[1] = (5, 10):  s1 15 s2 0  s3 28, cs 16
#   cycle 3: i=2 k=0  -> pts[2] = (0, 20):  s1 15 s2 20 s3 28, cs 21
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: i k
outputs: s1 s2 s3 cs
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 7.3.2.1 (assignment of structured variables), 6.4.4.2, 6.4.4.3, table 10; ed.2 3.3.2.1
---
0 i=1 k=3 => s1=13 s2=0 s3=0 cs=14
1 i=3 k=-2 => s1=13 s2=0 s3=28 cs=29
2 i=1 k=5 => s1=15 s2=0 s3=28 cs=16
3 i=2 k=0 => s1=15 s2=20 s3=28 cs=21
